<title>TRINIDAD AND TOBAGO: CRICKET-INDIA V WEST INDIES ONE-DAY INTERNATIONAL SCOREBOARD.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-INDIA V WEST INDIES ONE-DAY INTERNATIONAL SCOREBOARD.</headline>
<text>
<p>PORT OF SPAIN, Trinidad, April 26 - Scoreboard of the first</p>
<p>limited overs one-day international between West Indies and</p>
<p>India at Queen's Park Oval on Saturday.</p>
<p>India</p>
<p>   S.Tendulkar c Browne b Ambrose	 44</p>
<p>   N.Sidhu lbw Ambrose			 5</p>
<p>   R.Dravid c Hooper b Rose		 17</p>
<p>   M.Azharuddin b Rose			 3</p>
<p>   A.Jadeja c Browne b Rose		 19</p>
<p>   N.Mongia b Ambrose			 29</p>
<p>   R.Singh c Williams b Bishop	     2</p>
<p>   A.Kumble c Hooper b Adams		14</p>
<p>   S.Joshi b Ambrose			   8</p>
<p>   A.Kuruvilla not out			 3</p>
<p>   V.Prasad run out			    5</p>
<p>   Extras (lb5, w20, nb5)		   30</p>
<p>   Total (all out - 48.3 overs)	  179</p>
<p>Fall of wickets: 1-40, 2-65, 3-71, 4-86, 5-119, 6-123, 7-154,</p>
<p>8-171, 9-172.</p>
<p>Bowling: Ambrose 9.3-0-36-4 (nb3, w4), Bishop 7-0-38-1 (nb2,</p>
<p>w6), Walsh 8-0-34-0 (w2), Rose 10-2-25-3 (w4), Hooper 10-1-33-0</p>
<p>(w4), Adams 4-1-8-1.</p>
<p>West Indies</p>
<p>  S.Williams c Prasad b Kumble	   14</p>
<p>  S.Chanderpaul c Kuruvilla b Prasad   83</p>
<p>  B.Lara not out			     25</p>
<p>  C.Hooper not out			    9</p>
<p>  Extras					 18</p>
<p>  Total (for 2 wickets - 27.5 overs)  149</p>
<p>Fall of wickets: 1-43 2-132</p>
<p>Did not bat: J.Adams, R.Holder, C.Browne, I.Bishop,</p>
<p>C.Ambrose, F.Rose, C.Walsh.</p>
<p>Bowling: Prasad 7-1-35-1 (w2), Kuruvilla 4.5-0-27-0 (nb1,</p>
<p>w1), Kumble 4-0-23-1 (w4), Singh 5-0-25-0, Joshi 4-0-19-0,</p>
<p>Tendulkar 3-0-11-0 (w1).</p>
<p>West Indies won by 8 wickets after being set a revised</p>
<p>target of 146 off 33 overs after rain delayed play.</p>
<p>Man-of-the-match: Shivnarine Chanderpaul</p>
</text>
